WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.560
- You asked me to react to
this great challenge video.

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.358
Well, let's do it.

00:00:04.358 --> 00:00:05.400
Ooh!

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.030
Damn!

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:10.490
Yeah. So, the guy is on a
crate minding his own business.

00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:12.890
Then this little kid comes
around the guy pleads with him

00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.440
not to do anything to the crates

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.570
and the kid just kicks it
right out from under him.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.240
That is, that is mean.

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.390
So, the question is, is this kid liable?

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.770
And the answer is almost certainly yes.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:26.460
You can hold children
liable for negligence.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:29.590
You just have to use the
standard of a reasonable child.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.170
And if you're talking
about intentional torts,

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:32.630
the answer is probably yes too.

00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:34.800
I was actually preparing
for my law school class,

00:00:34.800 --> 00:00:36.760
when I was reminded of a very famous case

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:37.920
called Garratt versus Dailey.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.240
Involved an intentional tort.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.100
In the Dailey case,

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:42.850
a small child takes a
chair away from an adult

00:00:42.850 --> 00:00:44.300
before they sit down and they fall.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:45.133
And the question was,

00:00:45.133 --> 00:00:47.240
even if the kid didn't intend
for the fall to happen,

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.895
if there is a substantial
certainty that it will,

00:00:48.895 --> 00:00:50.180
then you're still liable.

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:53.000
Here, this kid seems to
know exactly what he's doing

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.150
and is almost certainly guilty

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.795
of intentional tort of battery
for kicking out those crates.

00:00:57.795 --> 00:00:58.628
Ouch!

